{"id": "EUVD-2026-103048", "enisaUuid": "37f8495a-d04f-30cc-ba88-28920dc21030", "description": "Webreaper Damselfly through 4.5.3 contains an authentication bypass vulnerability that allows unauthenticated attackers to access all /api/* routes because controller authorization attributes are commented out. Attackers can send PUT /api/users with Admin roles to create administrator accounts, or POST /api/users to reset any user's password, gaining full control.", "datePublished": "2026-10-16T17:39:01", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-16T21:19:19", "baseScore": 9.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@hieuPenguinnn/damselfly-api-missing-authorization", "https://github.com/Webreaper/Damselfly/blob/4.5.3/Damselfly.Web.Server/Controllers/UserManagementController.cs#L8-L53", "https://github.com/Webreaper/Damselfly/blob/4.5.3/Damselfly.Web.Server/Program.cs#L238-L242", "https://github.com/Webreaper/Damselfly/issues/409", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/webreaper-damselfly-through-4.5.3-missing-authentication-on-rest-api-controllers"], "aliases": ["GHSA-p952-wg9v-vp35", "CVE-2026-111626"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.45, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "f418dfd6-1a58-378c-8b0f-81836b8519b0", "product": {"name": "Damselfly", "vendor": {"name": "Webreaper"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22644.5.3"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "9a49b492-7dc9-3041-94c6-439c1baf7243", "vendor": {"name": "Webreaper"}}], "isExploited": false}